<section class="tab-pane fade p-3 p-md-4" id="<%= key %>-bad" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="<%= key %>-bad-tab" tabindex="0">
  <div class="row g-4 align-items-stretch">
    <div class="col-12 col-xl-7 order-2 order-xl-1">
      <div class="showcase-preview demo-bad demo-bad-<%= key %> h-100">
        <%= render bad_design_partial %>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-12 col-xl-5 order-1 order-xl-2">
      <aside class="showcase-takeaway showcase-takeaway-bad h-100 p-3 p-lg-4 rounded-4">
        <h3 class="h5 mb-3">Why it’s hard to use</h3>
        <% if key == "inputs" %>
          <ol class="demo-behavior-list">
            <li>Changing what people type destroys trust and makes errors hard to fix.</li>
            <li>Tiny controls turn a simple task into a precision test.</li>
            <li>Unlabeled choices force people to guess.</li>
            <li>An action that cannot be used is not an action.</li>
            <li>A wall of identical buttons offers noise instead of direction.</li>
            <li>A control that changes on its own cannot be trusted.</li>
            <li>Rejecting the correct answer teaches people not to trust the form.</li>
            <li>Inconsistent labels compete for attention and erase hierarchy.</li>
            <li>Moving a target punishes anyone trying to use it.</li>
          </ol>
        <% else %>
          <p class="small mb-0"><%= description %></p>
        <% end %>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
